            <ArticleTitle>Analgesic and anti-inflammatory activity of Caryophyllene oxide from Annona squamosa L. bark.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>149-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.phymed.2009.05.016</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Caryophyllene oxide was isolated from an unsaponified petroleum ether extract of the bark of Annona squamosa and studied for its analgesic and anti-inflammatory activity. Caryophyllene oxide at the doses of 12.5 and 25mg/kg body wt. and unsaponified petroleum ether extract at a dose of 50mg/kg body wt. showed significant central as well as peripheral analgesic, along with anti-inflammatory, activity. These activities of caryophyllene oxide were comparable with the standard drug used in the respective experiments.</AbstractText>
